  "events": [],
  "notes": [
    "the record's altitude track is empty: a KML file holds tracks of positions, not an altimeter's record over time, so every value is a channel",
    "the file holds its KML document 3 times over, one after another, each the same: it is read once",
    "the log's zero is the first point the file times: `when` 2030-01-02T10:00:00.000+02:00",
    "`coordinates` read in meters, from the KML standard: OGC 07-147r2 states a tuple's altitude in meters, and 1 of the file's 1 tracks carry one",
    "`when` read in UTC, from the KML standard: 3 times state their zone, `Z` or an offset, as XML Schema's date-time allows"
